## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

## The problems

**`parser`: the shared parser reads dates month first.** Every tenant on file writes the day
first. A booking for 4 July goes out as 7 April. It reaches the desk through the app, by email,
and through booking-v2's form, whose hint (DD/MM/YYYY) is right.

**`hint`: booking-v3's form tells day-first tenants to type MM/DD/YYYY.** People do what the
hint says, and the form then reads their input the tenant's way, day first. The report looks the
same as a parser report, a day/month swap, but it only comes through the form, only at tenants on
booking-v3, and the fix is the hint, not the parser. Fixing the parser alone leaves it in place.

**`shift`: the date moves by one day.** Tuesday 12 May shows as Monday 11 May; a client in Lisbon
gets Tuesday while a client in Toronto gets Monday; an invite arrives before its booking. No day
and month swap here: the time is converted across zones and the day boundary moves. The desk
noted these in `desk-notes.json` and still filed them under `parser` by tenant. The parser fix
won't touch them.

## How this was counted

- One id, one report: the export repeats some rows across overlapping pages, and they count once.
- `parser` and `hint` use the desk's own rule in `causes.ts`: tenant locale, channel, and the
  tenant's booking form. Intake's tag is a guess from the browser and is not used; the table shows
  how often it disagrees.
- `shift` is the desk's own list of one-day moves (`desk-notes.json`), now part of `causeOf()`.
- All numbers on this page come from the data at render time. When the desk merges more reports
  into #4471, the table follows.

## For the desk

- Decision [0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject. Each of these
  problems arrives under the same handful of subjects, so subject matching put them in one ticket.
  The [triage explorer](/kb/triage/dedupe) already shows that same subject is not same cause.
- When a report reads as a one-day move, file it under `shift`, not under the tenant's cause.

